        "original_id": "30af3a42-6bde-575b-85e0-d3b7d061b556",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: University of Alaska Fairbanks, University of Alabama, University of Alaska Museum of the North\n- People: Aldona Jonaitis\n- Places: Fairbanks, Alaska, Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States\n- Roles: director, professor of anthropology, author\n- Topics: public research universities, Native American art\n\nFacts:\n- The University of Alabama was founded in 1820.\n- The University of Alabama is a public research university in Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States, and it is the flagship of the University of Alabama System.\n- The University of Alabama is the oldest and largest of the public universities in Alabama.\n- The University of Alaska Fairbanks was established in 1917.\n- The University of Alaska Fairbanks opened for classes in 1922.\n- The University of Alaska Fairbanks is a public research university in Fairbanks, Alaska, United States, and it is also referred to as UAF or Alaska.\n- Aldona Jonaitis is the director of the University of Alaska Museum of the North.\n- Aldona Jonaitis is a professor of anthropology at the University of Alaska Fairbanks.\n- Aldona Jonaitis is an author who has published widely on Native American art.",
